# E27 -- Does zeroing a vermin population entry stop that vermin appearing? This is the v5.9 Vermin panel's whole premise. Addendum 54 makes the test sharper than it was: two levers reach vermin and only one is safe — zeroing an ENTRY is the ordinary population mechanism, while zeroing a vermin's FREQUENCY is exactly what froze the game, since CREEPY_CRAWLER is a vermin and the only underground rotter. This arm zeroes entries only and never touches a frequency. A season on CTRL against an untouched control, two replicates each, tool disabled, counting live vermin objects by race.
run 20260918-172914 fort CTRL backup CTRL.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Legendary Dimension site 32 tiles 29..29,20..20 seed WILDERPOP1
commits: DwarfCron 835fddb seasonal-wildlife 41bbd19 fps cap 1000

## Predictions (written before the run)
- entries gate vermin: the zeroed arm ends with markedly fewer live vermin objects and fewer distinct races than the control
- vermin ignore the entry, as cavern life ignores it: both arms carry the same vermin; the entry is bookkeeping and the Vermin panel needs a different lever
- vermin are seeded once at embark: both arms hold whatever the map started with and neither gains new races — the same shape E20 found for water

